.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt SEND 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm send
.Nd send a scheme-server reply
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x69).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
completes a request returned by
.Xr recv 2 .
The reply packet is version 1 and has an appended attachment tail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
u32 attach_count
struct { u32 handle; u32 rights_mask; } attach[attach_count]
.Ed
.Pp
All fields are little-endian.  At most four attachments are accepted.
Each
.Va handle
is looked up in the replying server's table and must carry
.Dv TRANSFER .
The kernel installs a duplicate in the requesting client's table with rights equal to the server
handle rights intersected with
.Va rights_mask .
A zero mask means all current source rights.
.Pp
For replies other than the
.Dv REPLY_HANDLE
form of
.Xr open 2 ,
the client reply buffer contains the inline data bytes followed immediately by
.Va attach_count
little-endian pairs of the client-table handle and the original rights mask.
The caller must reserve eight bytes per attachment after the data.
For a read reply, the data length is the reply's
.Va buffer_len ;
for Call and Fstat replies it is the inline
.Va data_len .
.Pp
The kernel validates every attachment before taking the client handle-table lock.
If destination insertion or reply-buffer delivery fails, it removes any attachments already
installed for that reply.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
